WEBVTT

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:34.430
"Operation: Infiltrate a Planetoid Base"

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:45.030
They're fast! I can't process
their data quick enough!

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:47.240
My unit feels heavy!

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.560
Did it get fat?! Did it?!

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:51.860
There is gravity since we're on Earth!

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:54.360
Crap! I can't keep up with them!

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:55.710
Guys, get your acts together!

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:58.390
Your controls will go
bonkers if you panic!

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:00.430
Right back at you!

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:04.420
Isn't that Team Rabbits?

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:06.420
Supposedly their AHSMB
units are under repair.

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:09.260
Since they're still considered students,
they're getting a supplementary lesson.

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:11.610
Is it just me, or do they
suck even worse now?

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:13.260
Who're the other three?

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:14.760
Probably teachers.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:16.640
Students can't pull
off moves like those.

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:19.980
I've gotta do something!

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:20.990
Now that it's come to this...!

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:24.020
Shining Miracle Turn Smash!

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:27.690
What gives?

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:29.320
What the hell was that?

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:31.040
And here I put my faith in you!

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:32.880
Fine! I'll charge ahead!

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:38.290
Whoo boy...

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:40.380
Their formation is a mess...

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:51.700
What the heck was that Miracle-whatever?

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:52.900
My secret move.

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:56.650
Yeah, figures. Most heroes
have a secret move, don't they?

00:02:56.890 --> 00:02:57.740
I know, right?

00:02:57.740 --> 00:02:59.400
We don't need one!

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:02.190
But heroes use secret
moves to save the day.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:03.850
I was sure I could pull it off...

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:07.910
If all we needed was confidence,
we'd get 100's studying by ourselves!

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:10.290
I never got to show my stuff...

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:12.360
Yo!

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:14.920
You weren't looking too
hot out there, huh?

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:19.210
Freakin' out after
that string of losses?

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:24.350
Your training session is over.

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:26.450
Team Rabbits, everyone
is to submit your

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:28.690
own personal analysis on why you lost.

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:32.920
Assemble in the Meeting Room in 30 minutes
with Team Doberman.

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:33.770
Over.

00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:35.540
See ya later.

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:39.840
Sirs, thank you for the lesson!

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:45.300
That's Team Doberman for ya!

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:46.690
They're scary!

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:48.950
Weren't they also students here?

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:50.940
Supposedly they were
highly accomplished.

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:53.650
A joint meeting...

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:56.000
Does that mean we're working with them
on our next mission?

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.690
That'd be super awesome!
All three dudes are stud muffins!

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:01.400
I'm amazed you can act so carefree

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:03.570
after nearly getting killed in that last mission.

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:06.010
Fear and romance are
two different things!

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:07.280
Man!

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.770
I guess the Fail Five are
still the Fail Five, huh?

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:13.320
How come they get to pilot
cutting-edge fighters?

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:22.980
My entrance may come
surprisingly soon...

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:29.530
I thought my Likeability Stats would go up
after becoming a wee bit famous.

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:31.730
You can't blame them
for feeling that way.

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:35.660
When you get down to it,
our team only won that very first battle.

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:38.030
They're blasting us on
the internet again...

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:41.130
Don't bring that up.
You'll give me another ulcer.

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:44.240
Your AHSMB units have
been fully repaired.

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:46.080
You will be transferring
to Star Rose tomorrow.

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:49.380
Upon arrival, we will
commence a co-op mission.

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:51.600
What's the matter?

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:56.300
Ma'am, what if we fail again...?

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:59.510
Thinking like that will only hinder
your performance!

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:02.460
You'll be fine!

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:04.800
This time you've got
Team Doberman with you.

00:05:08.310 --> 00:05:10.060
Lt. Commander, I have a question!

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:12.330
I've been meaning to
ask this for some time.

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:13.540
Go ahead, Lieutenant.

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:18.580
Please tell me your personal address
and when you're off duty.

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:22.450
Randy, we're in the middle of a meeting!

00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:24.580
You shouldn't ask such
shameless questions.

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:26.290
Don't be such a stiff!

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:28.200
If ya don't ask stuff
like this when you can,

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:29.720
you could forever miss the boat!

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:31.500
With you as our clown of a leader,

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:34.340
people keep calling
us the "Bummer Three,"

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:36.690
the "Comedic Three" and "Trio Dobermans."

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:38.380
The "Bummer Three"?

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:40.540
Just what I'd expect from our seniors!

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:42.600
What's wrong with being
the Bummer Three?!

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:45.640
And why do you always act
like you're better than me?!

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:48.100
Just because we're classmates
doesn't mean you can walk all over me!

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:51.060
It's the sub-leader's job to guide
the leader down the right path.

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:52.700
What are you, the
disciplinary committee?!

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:53.930
<i>Pardon?</i>

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:55.480
<i>Why must you always act so cool?!</i>

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:57.460
<i>What are you going on about
in the middle of a meeting?</i>

00:05:57.650 --> 00:05:59.120
<i>Do you think you're on
the Cool Committee?!</i>

00:05:58.490 --> 00:05:59.790
Sorry, but I don't have time to play.

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:00.540
<i>You should try to act a
bit more like a leader!</i>

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:01.210
Wh-what?!

00:06:02.770 --> 00:06:05.790
If there are no further questions,
this meeting is adjourned.

00:06:11.290 --> 00:06:14.640
I'm sorry. My team
always acts like this.

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:16.430
I-I see...

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:19.350
Quit acting like you're
excluded from our antics!

00:06:17.170 --> 00:06:19.350
Ow, that hurts! Randy!

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:21.180
I give up! Uncle, uncle!

00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:23.360
Thank God they aren't
as scary as I thought.

00:06:22.870 --> 00:06:24.080
What was that? I couldn't hear you?

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:25.760
In fact, they're funny.

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:25.720
You want me to stop?

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:28.300
But they're still cool!

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:30.030
And they saved our hides!

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:32.460
They're totally the hero type!

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:35.020
I'll really let you have it next time!

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:36.650
I swear, you never change!

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:37.690
Neither do you!

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:48.750
Excuse me! Thank you
for saving me the other day.

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:51.960
Uh, aren't you Red 5's pilot...?

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:53.140
I'm Izuru Hitachi.

00:06:56.210 --> 00:07:01.060
It feels like ages
since I was here last.

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:04.320
You've got it rough, huh?

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:07.280
They're sending you out hunting
when you're still just a student.

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:12.790
People are gonna say what they're gonna say;
don't worry 'bout it.

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:14.560
But I do!

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:17.240
Whenever I get sent to battle,
I wonder if I'm doing enough.

00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:21.030
You've survived this far!
Isn't that good enough?

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:23.470
But I want to become a hero!

00:07:24.070 --> 00:07:24.920
A hero?

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:34.670
So? Why do you want to
be a hero of all things?

00:07:34.670 --> 00:07:36.290
Because I think they're great!

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:38.070
I-I see...

00:07:42.010 --> 00:07:43.180
All right.

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:46.160
I'll tell you what it takes
to be a hero. You must be...

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:48.400
...good looking!

00:07:48.850 --> 00:07:49.560
Good looking?

00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:51.100
Right, it's all about the looks!

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:53.570
To be a hero, you gotta
be the best looking

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:55.620
member in your group and get all of the girls.

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:57.330
Aren't I a prime example?

00:07:57.600 --> 00:07:59.440
Y-yeah...

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:01.080
For the record, you...

00:08:02.990 --> 00:08:06.780
Yeah, you aren't as handsome as me,
but you're plenty good looking!

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:09.700
Don't worry, you'll
become an amazing hero.

00:08:09.700 --> 00:08:11.370
I guarantee it!

00:08:11.370 --> 00:08:13.300
Is-is that right...?

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:20.810
Let's see, what else is there...?

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:24.430
Well, I suppose you could say
that a hero has three jobs:

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:29.020
Making decisions, never giving up
and believing in your comrades.

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:32.310
Do you trust them... your friends?

00:08:35.090 --> 00:08:38.780
I watched the footage from all of
Team Rabbits' battles so far.

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:41.840
You try to do everything yourself while

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:44.200
desperately fighting to protect your friends.

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:47.990
You can't keep a team together
if you don't believe in your men!

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:50.210
Now putting that aside!

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:53.890
The pilots for Unit 2 and Unit 3...

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:55.380
Which do you have your sights set on?

00:08:55.790 --> 00:08:56.620
Pardon?

00:08:56.620 --> 00:09:00.170
Aren't they both adorable?
Which is your type?

00:09:00.170 --> 00:09:02.920
Or are you already dating one of them?!

00:09:02.920 --> 00:09:05.140
I-I couldn't possibly!

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:07.390
We're a team, so that
sort of stuff is taboo!

00:09:07.390 --> 00:09:08.680
What?!

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:12.600
I can't believe my ears!
Just how old are you guys?

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:17.840
Kei, Suruga and I are 16.
Asagi is 17. Tamaki is 15.

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:19.930
These are the best days of your life!

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:23.110
You gotta fall in love,
squabble and then break up!

00:09:23.110 --> 00:09:24.650
I really can't do that!

00:09:24.650 --> 00:09:27.450
I know! Swap teams with me.

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:31.920
As of today, you're Team Doberman's leader;
I'm taking Rabbits.

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:33.080
What?!

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:35.300
Of course, I'm just pulling your leg.

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:37.910
Your eyes looked kinda serious...

00:09:38.330 --> 00:09:39.350
Listen.

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:42.770
In our line of work, you never know
when you're gonna die.

00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:45.010
Wouldn't you like someone to remember

00:09:45.010 --> 00:09:47.030
who you were after you're gone?

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:50.750
Interact with as many people
as you possibly can.

00:09:51.260 --> 00:09:54.690
And make sure you remember
each person you meet along the way.

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:01.400
You can borrow this.

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:04.160
Study this with the pilots
for Unit 1 and Unit 4.

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:07.150
Does it contain footage
from our battles?

00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:08.520
Close enough.

00:10:12.030 --> 00:10:13.500
Watch this and put your
best foot forward!

00:10:14.530 --> 00:10:15.340
I will!

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:21.330
Let's watch this together!

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:23.510
What is it? Does it
contain video records?

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:26.800
Yep! He said to only watch it
with Asagi and Suruga,

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:28.140
but I figured we could
all watch it together!

00:10:34.140 --> 00:10:35.570
What is this...?

00:10:37.520 --> 00:10:38.480
That hurt...!

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:40.100
What the hell are you thinking?!

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:43.030
Well, this isn't exactly
what I was expecting...

00:10:46.530 --> 00:10:47.940
Pro wrestling?

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:53.380
Wh-what? What?
Wh-what's the big deal?!

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:56.020
This is a bit much for me...

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:59.710
Why are you freaking out when you're
the one constantly flirting with the ladies?

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:03.390
B-but this is on a totally
different level...

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:07.420
I'm gonna pass!

00:11:07.880 --> 00:11:11.090
Damn it! If we get caught,
reports will be the least of our worries.

00:11:11.090 --> 00:11:12.510
But I didn't mean-

00:11:12.510 --> 00:11:14.400
Enough! This is truly ridiculous.

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:20.480
I just realized something important.

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:22.410
What is it?

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:26.510
This actress resembles
Instructor Suzukaze.

00:11:28.030 --> 00:11:29.870
Now that you mention
it, I can see that...

00:11:36.780 --> 00:11:38.740
I can't bear to watch!

00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:42.370
The mission's name is
Operation: MacLean.

00:11:42.370 --> 00:11:48.180
You are to infiltrate the enemy base on
Planetoid RA221 and blow it up.

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:52.140
Concentrate!

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:56.140
Sir, what do you think
has gotten into them?

00:11:56.140 --> 00:11:57.400
Beats me.

00:11:57.890 --> 00:11:59.810
We don't know what to
expect once you're in.

00:11:59.810 --> 00:12:01.600
Although it isn't terribly big,

00:12:01.600 --> 00:12:04.520
we believe the base's
artificial gravity device is active.

00:12:04.520 --> 00:12:08.040
We have outfitted your units
for fighting in gravity.

00:12:08.360 --> 00:12:10.730
Was our training on
Earth before the mission

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:12.620
meant to serve as a simulation?

00:12:13.070 --> 00:12:16.990
It is far enough away from the battlefield
that we expect minimal security.

00:12:16.990 --> 00:12:19.260
However, with weak transmission signals,

00:12:19.260 --> 00:12:21.260
it will be impossible to communicate with us.

00:12:21.590 --> 00:12:23.590
Gold 4 will be in charge of the bomb.

00:12:23.940 --> 00:12:26.470
You will also use Gold 4's
computer to detonate it.

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:29.040
This mission came out
of nowhere, didn't it?

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:31.800
I can't believe we're destroying
a base that's on the sidelines.

00:12:32.760 --> 00:12:35.760
They're probably trying to make
the other team look good.

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:38.530
That's what it'd take
to save the MJP's face.

00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:42.890
At any rate, they want evidence
that we're winning.

00:12:43.230 --> 00:12:46.490
I bet this is a co-op to increase
the chances of success.

00:12:46.810 --> 00:12:49.370
Yeah, but do you think
we can handle this...?

00:12:50.470 --> 00:12:52.450
Did you end up watching
that video last night?

00:12:53.530 --> 00:12:56.050
Not me! I didn't watch it!

00:12:56.050 --> 00:12:58.660
Kei, are you going to
tell the instructor...?

00:12:58.660 --> 00:13:00.370
No, I wouldn't do that!

00:13:02.830 --> 00:13:05.150
D-don't worry, Kei!

00:13:05.150 --> 00:13:07.010
I'm sleepy after staying up all night,

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:08.470
but it was really refreshing.

00:13:11.280 --> 00:13:13.630
Well? Was it a good picker upper?

00:13:13.630 --> 00:13:17.090
Yeah, but I wound up showing it
to Kei and Tamaki...

00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:20.790
What?! Y-you've got some balls!

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:24.240
I'm amazed you've treaded grounds
far more dangerous than I have!

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:26.670
G-gee, thanks...

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:44.540
Identifying the enemy base.

00:13:44.540 --> 00:13:46.020
I'm forwarding the image.

00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:51.100
What's going on here?!

00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:53.470
Weren't we expecting minimal security?

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:56.850
What should we do?
Withdraw and request new orders?

00:13:57.280 --> 00:13:59.260
We can't reach our commanding officers.

00:13:59.260 --> 00:14:00.980
We'll have to make the
call for ourselves...

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:05.040
Let's carry out the mission!

00:14:05.930 --> 00:14:08.640
If the base is crowded with enemies
when it shouldn't be,

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:10.580
it means they're up to something.

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:12.360
We can't go back empty-handed!

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:13.370
Roger!

00:14:15.860 --> 00:14:17.620
Crap! They found us.

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:21.120
But how? Do they have eyes and ears?

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:22.320
We'll take them on!

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:24.060
My team will draw the enemy fire

00:14:24.060 --> 00:14:26.950
while your team carries out the mission!

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:29.090
But will you be okay?!

00:14:29.090 --> 00:14:31.010
Don't worry about us!

00:14:31.460 --> 00:14:33.640
There should be a gravity reactor
at the center of the base.

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:34.930
Set the bomb there.

00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:37.480
You'll do fine as long
as you remain calm.

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:45.260
They want us to infiltrate
the base by ourselves...?

00:14:45.260 --> 00:14:47.650
My feet absolutely refuse to move!

00:14:48.310 --> 00:14:49.740
Don't run away!

00:14:52.670 --> 00:14:57.110
Use your willpower to rein in the
JURIA-SYSTEM's survival instincts!

00:14:57.440 --> 00:14:58.370
Go!

00:14:58.780 --> 00:14:59.950
Y-yes, sir!

00:14:59.950 --> 00:15:01.580
Let's go, Red 5!

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:03.370
L-let's fight!

00:15:03.370 --> 00:15:04.770
Follow me, Purple 2!

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:06.510
H-hey, wait!

00:15:09.990 --> 00:15:12.550
What'll we do if they find us again?

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:15.540
Doberman is attracting all
of the enemy's attention.

00:15:15.540 --> 00:15:19.480
We'll be fine... I think... maybe.

00:15:28.960 --> 00:15:33.280
It looks like the base's guards
still don't know we're here.

00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:35.780
I bet we could get in through there.

00:15:38.070 --> 00:15:40.400
Rose 3 can't fit through that entrance.

00:15:40.400 --> 00:15:41.860
What?!

00:15:41.860 --> 00:15:44.380
What should we do, Izuru?
Leave Tamaki behind?

00:15:44.740 --> 00:15:46.670
Make up your mind before
the gate closes!

00:15:49.290 --> 00:15:50.250
I'll stay behind.

00:15:50.250 --> 00:15:51.590
Asagi...!

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:55.130
We'll probably need to shoot down
any enemy fighters that come back.

00:15:55.130 --> 00:15:57.100
Don't worry. We can handle it!

00:15:59.420 --> 00:16:00.430
Thank you.

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:02.520
Kei, Suruga, let's go!

00:16:14.800 --> 00:16:16.700
So this is a Wulgaru base...

00:16:19.110 --> 00:16:23.090
I'm detecting a reactor located
250 meters below us.

00:16:23.090 --> 00:16:26.320
If we blow that up, it should
take out the entire base.

00:16:26.320 --> 00:16:27.450
And the route?

00:16:27.450 --> 00:16:28.660
Straight ahead.

00:16:29.370 --> 00:16:30.710
Enemy fighters incoming at 2:00!

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:34.680
Suruga, protect the bomb!

00:16:34.930 --> 00:16:37.330
Kei, can you activate
the defense shields?

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:40.680
I could, but they'll make scanning
and analyzing the area that much harder.

00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:42.640
Got it. Then we'll plow
through without them!

00:16:55.980 --> 00:16:58.160
Good thing we trained on Earth!

00:16:59.820 --> 00:17:01.580
Take the upcoming 90°
turn to the right!

00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:17.050
Next drop 90° vertically down!

00:17:28.590 --> 00:17:31.320
The heat values are higher
than I had anticipated.

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:35.200
The sudden fluctuation in heat is beginning
to interfere with my sensors.

00:17:35.590 --> 00:17:37.180
Can you at least tell
what direction it's in?

00:17:37.690 --> 00:17:42.610
If we follow the artificial gravity pipeline,
we should reach the source.

00:17:42.610 --> 00:17:45.910
Doesn't that mean we're gonna keep
falling for who knows how long?!

00:18:01.590 --> 00:18:04.100
They aren't holding back even though
we're inside their base!

00:18:04.800 --> 00:18:05.710
That's a given!

00:18:05.710 --> 00:18:08.350
If we destroy this reactor,
it'll send the whole base sky high!

00:18:09.810 --> 00:18:11.760
It got hit somewhere along the line!

00:18:11.760 --> 00:18:13.600
Crap! I can't set it like this.

00:18:13.600 --> 00:18:14.400
What?!

00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:16.740
The mission's a failure!
We gotta retreat. Retreat!

00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:18.910
What should we do, Izuru?

00:18:19.210 --> 00:18:20.160
Izuru!

00:18:22.020 --> 00:18:24.410
Suruga, can you fix it?

00:18:25.640 --> 00:18:28.490
I don't think it's beyond me...

00:18:28.490 --> 00:18:29.080
Then do it!

00:18:29.650 --> 00:18:32.500
We won't make it back alive
if we don't destroy this base.

00:18:33.070 --> 00:18:35.670
This is our only option if
we hope to survive this!

00:18:35.910 --> 00:18:37.410
Are you serious?!

00:18:37.410 --> 00:18:38.590
Suruga, you can do it!

00:18:38.910 --> 00:18:40.300
I believe in you!

00:18:46.300 --> 00:18:46.890
Izuru!

00:18:47.340 --> 00:18:49.310
Kei, use your shields to protect Suruga.

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:50.520
I'll distract the enemy!

00:18:53.930 --> 00:18:56.470
Darn! I guess this is the only way.

00:19:04.190 --> 00:19:06.450
We're going to survive... Everyone is!

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:20.620
I wonder if everyone's okay...

00:19:20.960 --> 00:19:21.800
Yeah...

00:19:22.420 --> 00:19:23.810
They'll come back safe and sound.

00:19:24.380 --> 00:19:26.540
Otherwise my stomach will kill me!

00:19:46.320 --> 00:19:48.450
Hurry up, Suruga! Izuru is...!

00:20:02.430 --> 00:20:05.010
It's all set! I'm a genius!

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:06.220
Great! Now let's withdraw.

00:20:15.590 --> 00:20:16.440
It worked!

00:20:16.440 --> 00:20:17.690
Sweet!

00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:19.280
The secondary explosions
are going off fast!

00:20:19.620 --> 00:20:21.320
We'll get caught in the
blast if we don't hurry!

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:25.320
Why?! What type of
energy are they using?!

00:20:36.990 --> 00:20:37.960
We won't make it...!

00:21:01.930 --> 00:21:02.990
I suddenly accelerated!

00:21:05.810 --> 00:21:08.700
The instinct to survive
means serious business!

00:21:08.980 --> 00:21:10.410
Tamaki, thank you!

00:21:11.010 --> 00:21:15.330
Honestly, you three are lost without me.

00:21:28.460 --> 00:21:29.500
Is everyone okay?

00:21:29.500 --> 00:21:30.310
Asagi!

00:21:36.260 --> 00:21:38.940
I was so sure I was
gonna die this time...

00:21:51.830 --> 00:21:53.410
Lookin' good there...

00:21:54.280 --> 00:21:55.610
Hero of the Day!

00:23:40.980 --> 00:23:55.990
"Graduation"
